From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0297: Wi-Fi: the RSSI bounds (auto-join threshold)

wifid reads APPLE80211_IOC 106 (IO80211: RSSI_MIN, RSSI_MAX, RSSI_THRESHOLD) as the device opens and
refuses to auto-join any network heard more weakly than the threshold. Unanswered, it was 0 dBm:
"Below minimum RSSI threshold" for every network, even at -64 dBm. Answered: min = the noise floor,
max -20, threshold -85 dBm.
---
 bsd/dev/sapphire_apple80211.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sapphire_apple80211.c b/bsd/dev/sapphire_apple80211.c
index 10b7fe5..8b5cdae 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sapphire_apple80211.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sapphire_apple80211.c
@@ -386,6 +386,20 @@ get(struct apple80211req *request)
 		kfree_data(answer, sizeof(*answer));
 		return error;
 	}
+	case 106: {                             /* 0297: the RSSI bounds: version, min, max, auto-join threshold */
+		/*
+		 * wifid reads them once, as the device opens (IO80211's dictionary RSSI_MIN, RSSI_MAX,
+		 * RSSI_THRESHOLD), and refuses to auto-join any network heard more weakly than the threshold
+		 * ("Below minimum RSSI threshold"). Unanswered, the threshold was 0 dBm: no network was ever
+		 * strong enough, and every join had to be made by hand.
+		 */
+		struct {
+			uint32_t version;
+			int32_t min, max, threshold;
+		} answer = { .version = 1, .min = NOISE_FLOOR_DBM, .max = -20, .threshold = -85 };
+
+		return give(request, &answer, sizeof(answer));
+	}
 	case 21:                                /* how the last join went (0: not over yet) */
 		lck_mtx_lock(&apple80211_lock);
 		request->req_val = (int32_t)join_result;
